{
  "_comment": [
    "Line-pricing scenarios for the shared pricing module (issue #8).",
    "Expected amounts are hand-calculated from the offers below, in integer",
    "SGD cents, so a change in the module's arithmetic fails a test rather",
    "than quietly rewriting the expectation. Data here is invented for testing",
    "and is not a curated retailer record.",
    "Scope is verified ordinary and unconditional sale prices, plus same-product",
    "multibuys: whole deals at the deal price, remaining packs at the unit price,",
    "and a deal that is not cheaper ignored (PR-03, section 4).",
    "Requests outside the supported range are a caller mistake rather than a",
    "pricing outcome, so they throw and are tested in line.test.ts instead.",
    "Retailer IDs are the contract's real IDs; every price is still invented.",
    "rice uses an unconditional sale price, to show priceKind passes through."
  ],
  "offers": {
